Let $M$ be a closed orientable 3-manifold that is a mod 2 homology 3-sphere (i.e., $H_*(M;\mathbb{Z}/2)\cong H_*(S^3;\mathbb{Z}/2)$), and let $G$ be a finite non-solvable group acting on $M$ by orientation-preserving diffeomorphisms. Denote by $O(G)$ the maximal normal subgroup of $G$ of odd order. It is known that $G/O(G)$ contains a normal subgroup $N$, with quotient $(G/O(G))/N$ either abelian or a 2-fold extension of an abelian group, such that $N$ is isomorphic to one of the following groups:

(i) $\mathrm{PSL}(2,q)$;
(ii) $\mathrm{PSL}(2,q)\times \mathbb{Z}_2$;
(iii) $\mathrm{SL}(2,q)\times_{\mathbb{Z}_2} C$, where $C$ is a finite solvable group with a unique involution and the central product is taken over the common central involution;
(iv) the unique non-split central extension $\widehat{A}_7$ of the alternating group $A_7$ by $\mathbb{Z}_2$;
(v) $\mathrm{SL}(2,q)\times_{\mathbb{Z}_2}\mathrm{SL}(2,q')$, the central product over the common central involution,

where $q,q'$ are odd prime powers strictly greater than $4$.

Determine, for each of the groups in the list (i)–(v):
(a) which of them actually admit an orientation-preserving action on some mod 2 homology 3-sphere;
(b) which of them occur as the orientation-preserving isometry group of a closed hyperbolic 3-manifold that arises as the 2-fold cyclic branched covering of $S^3$ along some knot.

